We already know, area of a parallelogram: base × height \(=b h\).
So, the formula for the area a triangle is \(\frac{1}{2}\) (base × height) \(=\frac{1}{2} b h\).
A property of the median of a triangle. From the above formula we reach a simple but beautiful conclusion about any of the medians of a triangle.

\begin{figure}
\includegraphics[alt={},max width=\textwidth]{https://cdn.mathpix.com/cropped/4cec7484-b4be-4c71-abd9-c86b8e70e6e7-153.jpg?height=410&width=565&top_left_y=756&top_left_x=226}
