Also, this formula can be used to find the sum of consecutive numbers such as \(25+26+27+\cdots+58\).

Note that \(25+26+27+\cdots+58=(1+2+3+\cdots+58)-(1+2+3+\cdots+24) =\mathrm{S}_{58}-\mathrm{S}_{24}=\frac{58 \times 59}{2}-\frac{24 \times 25}{2}=29 \times 59-12 \times 25=1711-300=1411\).

